  doi          = {10.4049/jimmunol.1700786},
  pmid         = {29127151},
  note         = {In mast cells, copper regulates an MITF:tryptase axis: copper overload decreased tryptase content/mRNA, copper starvation increased it. Copper status did NOT alter histamine storage or IgE-mediated degranulation. Refines (and partly contradicts) the simple copper->DAO->histamine model: copper's mast-cell link is via tryptase, not histamine. Raw certainty 0.60, in vitro -> discounted 0.24.},
